# Companion Board: what's new

**Three changes since the 19 Nov zip:**

1. The SD card log now records **battery voltage, current, and roll/pitch/yaw**.
2. **Yaw** can now be watched in Live Expressions, like roll and pitch.
3. You can choose **starting roll/pitch/yaw values when arming**, like the throttle starting at 1200.

**Files to replace:** `Core/Src/main.c`, `Core/Inc/sd_logger.h`, `Core/Src/sd_logger.c`

---

## ⚙️ Settings you can change

All of these are `#define` lines near the top of `main.c`. To change one, edit the number, rebuild and flash.
Use **Ctrl+F** with the setting name to find it. 🆕 marks settings added in this update.

### Stick feel

| Setting | Now | What it does |
|---|---|---|
| `STICK_SCALE_ROLL_PCT` | **20** | How much of the full range the roll stick uses. 20 means full stick sends only 1400–1600 (gentle). 100 means full range (1000–2000). |
| `STICK_SCALE_PITCH_PCT` | **20** | Same, for pitch |
| `STICK_SCALE_YAW_PCT` | **20** | Same, for yaw |
| `STICK_DEADBAND_US` | 25 | Tiny stick movements near centre are ignored (stops drift). Raise it if the drone creeps with sticks centred. |

### Stick hold (sticks keep their last push instead of springing back)

| Setting | Now | What it does |
|---|---|---|
| `STICK_HOLD_ENABLE` | **1** | **1:** let go of a stick and the drone keeps doing what you last pushed. **0:** normal, sticks return to centre. |
| `STICK_HOLD_ROLL` | 1 | Turn hold on (1) or off (0) for roll only |
| `STICK_HOLD_PITCH` | 1 | Same, for pitch |
| `STICK_HOLD_YAW` | 1 | Same, for yaw. A held yaw means constant spinning, so consider 0 for first flights. |
| `STICK_HOLD_MIN_PUSH_US` | 100 | How far you must push before it counts (500 = full stick, so 100 = 20%). Raise it if bumps set holds by accident. |

How hold works: push and let go, and it holds the furthest point you reached. Push the same way to set a new value. **Push the opposite way to return to centre.** Disarming clears everything.

### Arming and throttle

| Setting | Now | What it does |
|---|---|---|
| `THROTTLE_ARMED_START_US` | **1200** | Throttle jumps here half a second after arming. Keep it below the throttle where the drone lifts off. |
| 🆕 `ARMED_START_ROLL_US` | **1500** | Roll value the drone starts with after arming. 1500 = centre. Allowed range is **1400–1600** at 20% scale. |
| 🆕 `ARMED_START_PITCH_US` | **1500** | Same, for pitch |
| 🆕 `ARMED_START_YAW_US` | **1500** | Same, for yaw |
| `THROTTLE_RATE_US_PER_SEC` | 75 | How fast the throttle stick changes throttle. Lower means finer altitude control. |
| `THROTTLE_MAX_US` | 1500 | Throttle can never go above this, whatever the stick does. |
| `THROTTLE_ARM_HOLD_MS` | 500 | Throttle is held at minimum this long after ARM so Betaflight accepts the arm. **Leave as is.** |
| `PILOT_FAILSAFE_TIMEOUT_MS` | 500 | If the controller signal is lost this long, cut throttle and disarm. |

The `ARMED_START_*` values only work with stick hold on. They stay until you move that stick.

### Wind correction

| Setting | Now | What it does |
|---|---|---|
| `CORRECTION_KP_US_PER_DECIDEG` | 0.8 | How hard it pushes back per degree of tilt. Raise it for a stronger correction, lower it if it overshoots. |
| `CORRECTION_KD_US_PER_DPS` | 0.3 | How much it resists fast tilting. Raise it to damp wobble. |
| `CORRECTION_MAX_US` | 100 | Most the correction can ever move a stick (safety limit) |
| `CORRECTION_ATT_DEADBAND_DECIDEG` | 20 | Tilt under 2° is ignored |
| `CORRECTION_RATE_DEADBAND_DPS` | 15 | Rotation under 15°/s is ignored |
| `CORRECTION_STICK_DEADBAND_US` | 40 | If the pilot moves a stick more than this, the correction backs off that axis |
| `CORRECTION_ALWAYS_ON` | 0 | **1:** correction always on, ignoring the controller button (bench testing only) |

### Logging

| Setting | Now | What it does |
|---|---|---|
| `SD_LOG_ENABLE` | 1 | **1:** write a CSV file to the SD card. **0:** no SD logging. |
| `SD_LOG_EVERY_N_LOOPS` | 1 | 1 means a row every 20 ms (50 per second). 5 would be 10 per second (smaller files). |
| `LOG_CSV_ENABLE` | 1 | **1:** also print CSV rows on the serial terminal (needs a laptop on J7) |
| `LOG_CSV_EVERY_N_LOOPS` | 5 | Serial CSV every 5th loop (10 per second) |
| `STATS_ENABLE` | 1 | **1:** print correction off-vs-on statistics on the serial terminal |
| `STATS_PRINT_MS` | 5000 | How often the statistics print (ms) |
| `STATUS_PRINT_EVERY_N_LOOPS` | 50 | How often the status lines print (50 = once a second) |

### Battery and flight controller readings

| Setting | Now | What it does |
|---|---|---|
| `FC_EXTRA_POLL_ENABLE` | 1 | **1:** read battery, armed state and received channels from the flight controller. **Needed for voltage/current logging.** |
| `FC_EXTRA_POLL_EVERY_N_LOOPS` | 3 | How often to ask. Raise it if the loop starts running late. |
| `BATT_CUTOFF_ENABLE` | 0 | **1:** force a disarm when the battery gets too low |
| `BATT_CUTOFF_DECIV` | 0 | Low-battery cutoff in 0.1 V (e.g. 180 = 18.0 V). **Set it for your pack before turning the cutoff on.** |
| `BATT_CUTOFF_READS` | 5 | Low readings in a row needed before it trips (avoids false trips from voltage dips) |

### Controller setup (change only if the controller changes)

| Setting | Now | What it does |
|---|---|---|
| `INPUT_SOURCE` | `INPUT_LORA` | Where pilot input comes from: `INPUT_LORA` (our controller), `INPUT_CRSF` (ExpressLRS radio), `INPUT_NONE` (bench only) |
| `AXIS_LX_INVERT` | 1 | Flip yaw direction (set 1 if the drone yaws the wrong way) |
| `AXIS_RX_INVERT` | 1 | Flip roll direction |
| `AXIS_RY_INVERT` | 0 | Flip pitch direction |
| `BTN_ARM_IS_L3` | 1 | **1:** button 1 = ARM, button 2 = correction. **0:** swapped. |
| `THROTTLE_INTEGRATE` | 1 | **1:** throttle stick nudges throttle up/down and centre holds it. **0:** stick position = throttle. |

### Bench-test switches (keep at 0 for flying!)

| Setting | Now | What it does |
|---|---|---|
| `AUTO_ARM_AT_BOOT` | 0 | **1:** the board arms itself at startup. **Props off only.** |
| `//#define FLIGHT_TEST_ENABLE` | off | Remove the `//` to run the automatic strapped-down thrust test |

**Safety checks are built in.** If a setting is out of range (e.g. a start value the stick can't reach), the code **won't build** and tells you which setting to fix.

